.page rev 1 reverse the characters of each line

# SYNOPSIS
*rev* [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`rev` writes each line of its input backwards. It understands UTF-8: a multibyte character is kept whole. Standard input is read when no file is given.

# EXAMPLES
    echo abc | rev
    echo "reimu" | rev

# SEE ALSO
tac(1), tr(1)
